Title
-----

     iv -- Instrumental variable (IV) programs useful for one-sample Mendelian
randomization (MR) analyses

Syntax
------

        iv subcommand ...

    where subcommand is one of

    fsw         ivfsw
    lsmm        ivlsmm
    msmm        ivmsmm
    mw          ivmw
    tsps        ivtsps
    tsri        ivtsri
    xtile       ivxtile
    -------------------------------------------------------------------------

    and ... is the syntax of that command, including any weights, if, in, and
    options.

Description
-----------

    iv is a simple wrapper to the commands in the ivonesamplemr package.

    The subcommand is specified as the ivonesamplemr program name without its
    iv prefix, i.e. ivlsmm ... can alternatively be run using the syntax iv
    lsmm ....  Everything after the subcommand is passed unchanged to that
    command.

Options
-------

    iv takes the options for the specified subcommand.

Examples
--------

        . use
            https://raw.githubusercontent.com/remlapmot/ivonesamplemr/main/da
            > ta/ivbinoutdata, clear

    Fit the model with a single instrumental variable.

        . iv lsmm y (x = z1)

        . iv msmm y (x = z1 z2 z3)

        . iv tsps y (x = z1 z2 z3), link(logit)

        . iv tsri y (x = z1 z2 z3), link(logit)

    Sanderson-Windmeijer conditional F-statistics after ivregress.

        . ivregress 2sls y (x1 x2 = z1 z2 z3)

        . iv fsw

    Moving window and quantile analyses.

        . iv mw, window(2400) par(x): ivregress 2sls y (x = z1 z2 z3)

        . iv xtile, nq(4) par(x): ivregress 2sls y (x = z1 z2 z3)

Stored results
--------------

    iv returns the results from the specified subcommand.

